---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Shipping Policy"
  description="Cloud Peptides shipping policy — order minimums, shipping costs, and the customs replacement guarantee."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>Order requests, not accepted orders</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting an order through our cart is a <strong>request</strong>, not an accepted order or a
    completed purchase — see our <a href="/shop-terms">Shop Terms</a>. Nothing below describes a
    guaranteed shipment; it describes what happens once a request has been reviewed and accepted.
  </p>

  <h2>Order minimum and shipping cost</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Two-kit minimum per order.</li>
    <li>Shipping costs $15 for a two-kit order.</li>
    <li>Shipping is free for orders of three or more kits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Carrier, destinations, and timing</h2>
  <p>
    We confirm the carrier, delivery-region availability, and an estimated dispatch time directly
    with you when your order request is reviewed and accepted — not before, and not on this page. We
    are not going to state a carrier or a guaranteed delivery time here until it is real and
    accurate for your specific order.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for providing an accurate, complete shipping address and for complying with
    the import laws, taxes, and duties that apply in your destination. Laws governing research
    peptides vary by location — it is your responsibility to know and follow the laws that apply to
    you before ordering. See our <a href="/shop-terms">Shop Terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Customs replacement guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    If verifiable tracking information or official documentation shows that customs refused or
    returned your original package, we will provide <strong>one replacement shipment</strong> at no additional
    product or shipping charge, subject to the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Limited to one replacement shipment per order.</li>
    <li>
      This is a <strong>replacement</strong>, not a cash refund — see our
      <a href="/returns">Return and Refund Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      It applies only when reshipping is lawful. This guarantee is never a way to evade an import
      prohibition or customs enforcement, and we will not use it that way.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a shipping question about an order request, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we'll
    answer directly.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
